WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.790
- [Narrator] By now,
you've hopefully finished

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:04.250
all of "You," season
two but if you haven't,

00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:06.333
beware, there are spoilers ahead.

00:00:07.877 --> 00:00:11.767
- We can be together now.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:13.684
- I don't think we can.

00:00:15.621 --> 00:00:17.300
I think I broke you.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.370
- I'm fine.

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.253
- Listen to me,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.820
this is not your fault, this is not you.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:27.340
Everything I told you is true.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:32.340
Beck, Henderson, Delilah, I killed them,

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:36.810
their blood is on my hands.

00:00:39.401 --> 00:00:42.568
- Joe, you didn't kill Delilah, I did.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.330
- [Narrator] So, who
saw that twist coming?

00:00:50.330 --> 00:00:53.880
- [Joe] What the fuck?

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.280
- [Narrator] It turns out
Love is a better match for Joe

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.773
than he ever imagined.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.800
- I wolf you.

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:03.420
- I wolf you too.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.530
- [Narrator] The parallels between them

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:07.080
go all the way back to
their respective childhoods.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:13.383
- We both had to learn how
to survive really young.

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:16.573
How old were you the first time?

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.070
- Nine.

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:19.983
- I'm so sorry.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.320
- [Narrator] We hear
about Love and Forty's

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.310
rich yet troubled childhood
throughout the season.

00:01:25.310 --> 00:01:28.940
One story we keep returning to
is about an au pair they had

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.740
when their parents set up Anavrin.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:32.640
- The year my parents launched Anavrin

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:37.640
they left us with this
fucking crazy au pair.

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:41.190
Forty saw way too much too young.

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:46.190
The way Forty tells it,
she was his first love,

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.570
to this day he's not
acknowledge that it was abuse.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.350
- [Narrator] When Forty
unwittingly figures out

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.300
the real story about Beck's murder,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.600
while high on LSD,

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.450
he also tells Joe what
he believes is the truth

00:01:58.450 --> 00:01:59.670
about the au pair.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:02.563
- When I found out she was
seeing some college guy,

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:08.770
I felt this rage inside of me,

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:13.003
like an animal, made of teeth and of fire,

00:02:15.283 --> 00:02:20.283
then I blacked out and I killed her.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.950
I came to and I was standing over her.

00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:31.570
- [Narrator] But, by the end,
Love tells a different story.

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:36.570
- Forty was a child, she
was a rapist, I stopped her.

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.693
I protected Forty because I had to,

00:02:47.325 --> 00:02:48.475
'cause nobody else was.

00:02:49.506 --> 00:02:52.173
(intense music)

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:58.550
Better they thought it was him.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:00.743
Forty was blacked out, a victim.

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:03.310
- [Narrator] This is the first parallel

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:04.603
between Joe and Love.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.900
Joe's first kill was also at a young age,

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:11.420
he was just nine years old
when he shot his father.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.570
Fast forward to Joe and
Love's first meeting,

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:17.760
that in itself is the seasons first twist.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.980
- [Joe] Hello, you.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:22.370
No, fuck, no, I'm not doing that.

00:03:22.370 --> 00:03:23.720
- [Narrator] Joe leads
the audience to believe

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.430
it's your standard meet queue.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.493
- Do you think this
peach looks like a butt?

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:30.270
- [Narrator] That is until Joe reveals

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:33.080
at the end of episode one
that he's had his sights set

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:34.333
on Love all along.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.520
Now, there are few people in the show

00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.940
who can match Joe's level of obsession

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:44.320
but Love comes close.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.800
The way she talks about her
first impressions of him

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.670
mirror the way he talks about his victims

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:50.170
when he first encounters them.

00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.320
- And then I saw you,

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:58.270
I knew right away, in my gut,
I recognized something in you

00:03:58.270 --> 00:04:02.450
and hey, smart, sexy, funny,

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:06.783
a little darkness that made
you less story book, more real.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:09.740
I started to fantasize again.

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:11.575
- [Narrator] And it turns out,

00:04:11.575 --> 00:04:13.970
she too has a little stalker in her.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:15.673
- Maybe I got a little obsessed,

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.250
maybe I used my parents
means to do a little digging

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.593
after Candace left.

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.683
They owned me that much.

00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.400
- This is how she discovers Joe's cage,

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:30.823
which doesn't freak her
out in the slightest.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:35.030
- You were even smarter, more passionate,

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.180
more devoted than I'd known.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:38.950
- [Narrator] Even finding
out Joe killed Beck

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.520
doesn't seem to phase her.

00:04:40.520 --> 00:04:43.060
In fact, the way she
sees Beck mirrors the way

00:04:43.060 --> 00:04:44.930
Joe spoke about Benji,

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.450
Beck's hipster boyfriend from season one.

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:49.710
- [Joe] I do understand
something about you now, Beck,

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:53.310
you somehow think this
guy is all you deserve.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.510
- Guinevere Beck was
un-special and mediocre,

00:04:56.510 --> 00:04:58.710
she didn't deserve you.

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.020
- [Narrator] Once she finds
out about this dark side,

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:02.720
she tried to provoke it.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:04.950
In the episode "Ex-istential Crisis,"

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.870
Joe believes Love has moved on with Milo.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:09.240
But to hear Love tell it,

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:11.870
she was using him in
an attempt to coax out

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.763
his more murdery tendencies, yikes.

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:19.260
- If you could trust
me, show me your heart,

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.860
even the darkest parts,

00:05:21.860 --> 00:05:24.970
then we'd be starting our future
together on the right foot.

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:26.850
- [Narrator] Joe is
constantly making excuses

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:27.840
for his behavior,

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.653
generally claiming he
murders people for Love.

00:05:31.610 --> 00:05:33.690
This is something Love does too,

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.710
both for him and herself.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.810
- [Love] You did some terrible things

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:39.940
but that's what sensitive
people do when they're trapped

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.430
in a bad relationship.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:43.100
- [Narrator] This is why, she claims,

00:05:43.100 --> 00:05:45.120
she kills Delilah and Candace.

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:46.510
- [Love] I dealt with Delilah the same way

00:05:46.510 --> 00:05:47.763
I dealt with the au pair.

00:05:50.210 --> 00:05:52.310
I'm protecting you because I want to.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.350
- [Narrator] Even the way
she covers up her crimes

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:56.040
has echos of Joe.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.360
Watch how Love lays out
her plan to cover up

00:05:58.360 --> 00:06:00.140
Delilah and Henderson's murders.

00:06:00.140 --> 00:06:02.690
- We frame Ellie for Henderson's murder

00:06:02.690 --> 00:06:04.650
with an anonymous tip.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:06.390
Between the total lack of evidence

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:09.296
and the fact she's a 15-year-old girl,

00:06:09.296 --> 00:06:12.010
it instantly becomes a joke.

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:14.210
That's when Delilah's body will be found

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:15.970
with a suicide note,

00:06:15.970 --> 00:06:18.070
the shock waves will destroy the case,

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:20.780
Ellie will walk free with
settlement money for life.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.970
The investigation becomes poisoned

00:06:22.970 --> 00:06:25.230
and you are never mentioned in connection

00:06:25.230 --> 00:06:27.000
with Henderson again.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.590
- [Narrator] Doesn't it
sound a lot like something

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:29.883
Joe would come up with?

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:34.410
"You" is told mostly from
the prospective of Joe

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:36.260
and this entire twist is built around

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:38.860
the way he creates unrealistic versions

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:40.483
of the women he's obsessed with.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:43.310
- You know why this is happening?

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:48.293
Because while I was seeing
you, really seeing you,

00:06:49.130 --> 00:06:51.773
you were busy gazing
at a god damn fantasy.

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:58.040
A perfectly imperfect girl,
you saw what you wanted to see

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:06.370
but I was always right
here, the whole time.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:08.487
- [Narrator] But if you
go back to episode two,

00:07:08.487 --> 00:07:11.300
her dark side is definitely foreshadowed.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.360
As Joe cuts up Jaspers body,

00:07:13.360 --> 00:07:15.920
the scene is intercut
with Love preparing a meal

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:19.320
but more specifically,
cutting up a joint of meat.

00:07:19.320 --> 00:07:22.523
Love has always been more
like Joe than he ever knew.

00:07:23.533 --> 00:07:24.683
- We're soulmates, Joe.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:27.440
- [Narrator] But is that enough for him?

00:07:27.440 --> 00:07:30.190
The seasons ending suggests no.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:32.220
He's about to kill Love when she reveals.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:35.163
- No, I'm pregnant! (gasping)

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:40.370
- [Narrator] Joe is obsessed
with protecting children,

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:42.750
perhaps because of his
own troubled childhood,

00:07:42.750 --> 00:07:44.470
so the prospect of becoming a father

00:07:44.470 --> 00:07:46.573
is enough to save Love's life.

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:50.090
- Nothing is more important than this.

00:07:50.090 --> 00:07:52.090
- [Narrator] As the season
comes to a close, however,

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:54.910
it's clear this isn't enough for him.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:57.200
Love may be his murderous equal

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:00.080
but he sees suburban life
with her as a prison.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:02.800
- [Joe] Not ever Siberia is cold.

00:08:02.800 --> 00:08:06.670
Summer '73, it's sunny with
eco-conscious landscaping

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.980
and when I found myself here, locked in,

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.290
I thought this was the end.

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.410
- [Narrator] And it
seems he has his eyes set

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.910
on his next victim.

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:17.630
- [Joe] This is where I had to be,

00:08:17.630 --> 00:08:22.223
exactly where I had to be to meet you.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:25.743
See you soon, neighbor.

